  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 213 AM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nn upper level low to the south will continue to track eastward as a \nupper level ridge builds in from the west with strong southerly \nwinds keeping temperatures in the 50s. SFC winds will be the \nstrongest across northern Nebraska into north central Nebraska \nMonday and Tuesday with winds around 15 to 20 mph and gust up to 35 \nmph. On Wednesday a cold front will move into the area, ahead of the \nfront compressional heating will warm temperatures into the upper \n50s to low 60s across southwest Nebraska into north central \nNebraska, making Wednesday the warmest day of the week. There will \nbe a slight chance of scattered precipitation chances Wednesday\nafternoon and evening. Temperatures cool into the low 50s for \nThursday. \n\n\nAttention then turns to a system moving in to end the week Friday \nand Saturday. As the upper level low moves onshore into the western \nCONUS Friday and moves eastward increasing precipitation chances \nFriday. Will need to continue to monitor the system as models \nat this time are suggesting the system could potentially move \nacross the Central CONUS as a fairly strong closed low system, \nhowever as this is still pretty far out in the forecast and the \nsystem is still well offshore, the track and strength could \nstill change as we approach the end of next week. &&",
